<header class="resume-heading"><h1>Conor Brown</h1><p><strong>Staff Software Engineer · C#/.NET · Architecture & Platform Engineering</strong></p><p>Oklahoma, USA · <a href="mailto:carllbrown87@gmail.com">carllbrown87@gmail.com</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/conor--brown/">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://github.com/conorbrown-dev">GitHub</a></p></header>
<section><h2>Professional summary</h2><p>Staff-level software engineer with 12+ years of .NET experience who sets technical direction across teams, not just within one. Owns architecture for legacy modernization, domain-driven design adoption, cloud migration paths, and the engineering standards other engineers build against. Has delivered platform-scale systems (remote management across 2,000+ servers, billing telemetry under a 99.9% delivery SLA) and cut delivery-pipeline times by more than half. Multiplies the output of a 10-developer team through architecture reviews, design workshops, mentoring, and clear standards for validating AI-assisted code. Works across C#/ASP.NET Core, SQL Server, and Azure.</p></section>
<section><h2>Selected impact</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Architecture and modernization:</strong> Led the move of a legacy .NET Framework MVC application to .NET 10, and defined a coordinated path to Azure App Service covering runtime configuration, Entra integration, Key Vault identity, parallel pipelines, staging validation, and rollback planning.</li>
<li><strong>Domain-driven design adoption:</strong> Led event-storming and DDD sessions that made business rules and ownership explicit, then carried the model through aggregates, APIs, persistence, UI, and end-to-end tests in a DDD/CQRS workflow and rule-builder capability.</li>
<li><strong>Testing strategy:</strong> Drove the decision to keep end-to-end tests in the application repository rather than a separate test project, which cut overhead and complexity and kept tests from going stale as the application changed.</li>
<li><strong>Engineering standards:</strong> Wrote the <strong>CLAUDE.md</strong> reference guide covering DDD, dependency boundaries, modern C#, and a reference vertical slice; reinforced it through code reviews and workshops.</li>
<li><strong>Delivery performance:</strong> Reduced CI/CD duration from roughly <strong>40–60 minutes to 19 minutes</strong>, and core test execution from 8–9 minutes to approximately 21 seconds, through coverage-tooling changes.</li>
<li><strong>Business-critical platform work:</strong> Designed an Azure Service Bus usage-logging platform around a <strong>99.9% delivery SLA</strong>; it fed billing and revenue for the whole company and its enterprise customers. Also built remote management infrastructure serving <strong>2,000+ servers</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Technical leadership:</strong> Guide a team of 10 developers through design decisions, architecture reviews, and workshops; supported a product-line transition spanning catalog identity, component modeling, pricing, drawings, indexing, and admin tooling.</li>
</ul></section>
<section><h2>Professional experience</h2>
